# Entry Main. The same universal reference input `@: target Box` admits `Other`; the body is entered (its first line
# writes `Log\entered`), then the path `target\q` is reached and `Other` has no field `q`: the ordinary refusal of a
# reached path, after entry -- not a refusal at admission. `Log\entered` 1, `Log\after` 0; answer 3 (step 21.7 K2).
# Norm: the book #structural-call; L2_spec, reference places (a full requirement belongs in the typed head
# `Model@`, which this place is not); the ordinary rule of a reached path with an absent field.
Box:
    int: q 1
end: Box
Other:
    int: z 1
    int: w 2
end: Other
Log:
    int: entered 0
    int: after 0
end: Log
Add:
    @: target Box
    add:
        Log\entered := 1
        target\q := target\q + 10
    end: add
end: Add
Main:
    Add\add(target := Other)
    Log\after := 1
